Pista includes and interoperates with third-party software. Each third-party
component remains subject to its own license terms.

The Pista assembly preserves dependency-provided license, notice, and
dependency metadata under META-INF. Release candidates also include CycloneDX
software bills of materials for the JVM distribution. Those files are the
authoritative version-specific dependency inventory.
The JVM SBOM covers components shipped in the Pista assembly. Spark, Hadoop,
Scala, and their transitive dependencies are provided by the deployment and
must be inventoried and scanned with that external runtime.

Embedded third-party components
===============================

Apache Maven Wrapper
--------------------

The `mvnw` and `mvnw.cmd` scripts are derived from Apache Maven Wrapper 3.3.2,
https://github.com/apache/maven-wrapper/tree/maven-wrapper-3.3.2. Pista modified
their temporary-directory cleanup to preserve recoverability, checksum-tool
fallback for macOS, and Windows mirror URL mapping. They retain their Apache
License 2.0 headers. The upstream notice is:

Apache Maven Wrapper

Copyright 2013-2022 The Apache Software Foundation

This product includes software developed at
The Apache Software Foundation (http://www.apache.org/).

The original idea and initial implementation of the maven-wrapper module is derived
from the Gradle Wrapper which was written originally by Hans Dockter and Adam Murdoch.

Copyright 2007 the original author or authors.

Public Suffix List
------------------

Pista contains a fixed snapshot of the Mozilla Public Suffix List:

  Upstream: https://github.com/publicsuffix/list
  Source commit: e1b8015c3b2f0f4f8c18659c2480fc1a22c07b20
  Source path: public_suffix_list.dat
  License: Mozilla Public License 2.0

The upstream license notice is retained in the data file. Pista's provenance
record and checksum are documented in:

  pista-catalyst/src/main/resources/com/pista/spark/sql/catalyst/functions/PUBLIC_SUFFIX_LIST.md

Runtime and optional dependencies
=================================

Pista uses Apache Spark, Scala, ClickHouse JDBC, the Doris Spark connector,
Apache Iceberg, Lance, FreeMarker, AWS SDK, and
their transitive dependencies. Dependencies are not relicensed by Pista.
The source POM files, generated SBOMs, and dependency-provided META-INF notices
identify the exact versions and terms for a release candidate.
